WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.901
"Young Percival, no more than 15,


00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.236
from the safety of the thicket,


00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.247
watched the knights pass by.


00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.980
He perceived they served
a higher calling,


00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:23.015
<i>a calling he felt
stirring within him.</i>


00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:27.219
<i>Percival asked his mother permission
to journey to King Arthur's court</i>


00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.491
<i>and seek knighthood.</i>


00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:34.293
<i>His mother had long-feared
this moment would come," Sailor.</i>


00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:39.409
"Nonetheless, she gave her son
blessing to pursue his quest.


00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:45.737
But she warned him, he would
be tested beyond imagination.


00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:50.109
Be deprived, know pain and sadness.


00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.587
<i>Perhaps, never become a knight.</i>


00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:57.954
<i>Percival traveled to
King Arthur's court.</i>


00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.320
<i>There, he met rebuke and ridicule.</i>


00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:06.903
For he was not of noble birth,
nor did he possess skill of arms.


00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:11.897
<i>In secret, he studied the
ways of the knights.</i>


00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:15.033
<i>His plight caught the
eye of Sir Lancelot</i>


00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.475
who began to mentor him.


00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.276
<i>During Percival's
ordeal, the Red Knight</i>


00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:30.428
an incarnate of darkness,
sought to destroy the Grail.


00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:36.929
He lay waste to King Arthur's
knights, one by one.


00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:43.962
<i>Finally, it fell upon
slender Percival</i>


00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:47.201
<i>to face the Red Knight."</i>


00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:52.115
<i>And Sailor, "Percival had no fear."</i>


00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.106
Get up, Sailor!


00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.742
<i>"His years of hardship had
taught him how to suffer.</i>


00:02:56.743 --> 00:03:00.720
<i>He was ready in body,
mind and spirit.</i>


00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:07.821
<i>He would prove in life or death,
his worthiness in battle.</i>


00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:13.859
<i>Percival went forth
with joy in his heart.</i>


00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.864
<i>For this was what he wanted:
to be an instrument of peace.</i>


00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:25.641
<i>To be able to sacrifice all
in service of God and man."</i>


00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.837
Lead with your right, kid!


00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.991
Lay on him. Lay on him!


00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:22.272
- Get away from him.
- Let him go, let him go.


00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.831
Let's see some blood!


00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.410
Work the body!


00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.018
Kill him, Sailor!


00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.491
- Come on, let him go.
- Let's see some blood!


00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:47.154
You got him, kid! Take him down!


00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.726
You gotta throw back
here, let's go.


00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.497
Break it up, boy. Break it up!


00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.340
Stop the haymakers. Stop
the haymakers! Double up.


00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.108
Another fight, then, is it?


00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.789
Once more into the fray.


00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.425
Once more into the fray.


00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:19.157
You're a silly man.


00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.220
- It's okay, Mom.
- No, it's not okay.


00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:26.391
- I'm not gonna get hurt.
- Yes, you will. You're too old.


00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:29.300
- I'm in good shape.
- No, you're still old.


00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.997
I got one or two fights
left in me, right, Ma?


00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:35.236
No, you are used up and broken.


00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.271
I've never been knocked down.


00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:42.341
Heh. See, that's why you're broken.


00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:45.455
A man should know when
to go down. You don't.


00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.949
You never did.


00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.952
I never should have said it to you.


00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.153
Said what?


00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.223
That I want to go to
Ireland before it comes.


00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.732
You didn't, I did.


00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:02.000
You are such a liar.


00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.006
Anyways, loser's
purse will cover it.


00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.938
Oh. I see you're aiming high.


00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.417
Father Brennan wants
to talk to you.


00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.257
About what? And don't say God.


00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.588
About what's coming.


00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:27.023
I'm not afraid.


00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.533
You should pass in a
state of grace, Ma.


00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.001
You still believe, don't you?


00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.432
Yeah, I do.


00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:41.271
How can you after
what he did to you?


00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.575
Only a monster takes the innocent.


00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:48.351
If there is a God, it's a monster.


00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:52.277
A doer of evil and wicked things.


00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:55.580
I will not seek grace
from a monster,


00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.489
nor will a monster give it.


00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.196
Will you talk to Father Brennan?


00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:09.161
Maybe. If he takes off his robes
and shoves a crucifix up his arse.


00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:10.773
Maybe.


00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.666
Nice, Ma.


00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:18.045
- I'll ask him, see what he says.
- Good.


00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.742
Have you gone to see Albright?
Will he be there with you?


00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.710
- He can't be there.
- Why not?


00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:28.280
He's busy at Safe Hope.


00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.549
- I see.
- He's a good man.


00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.856
If he was a good man, he would
talk you out of this fight.


00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:37.564
No one's gonna talk me
out of the fight, Ma.


00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:43.764
- Lay it on, Sailor!
- You've already got the game!


00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:48.806
It's all you, Sailor. Come on!


00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.811
Use your jab, man. Use your jab.


00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:55.511
Come on, man. Come on! Come on.


00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.792
Back to your corners,
guys, let's go.


00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.293
- You're done.
- Yeah.


00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:18.763
Hey, kid. Get over here.
Come on, sit down.


00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.699
<i>Sailor! Sailor!</i>


00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:24.035
All right, come on, sit down.
You ain't got all day. Come on.


00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:27.172
<i>Sailor! Sailor! Sailor!</i>


00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:29.741
You wanna make it 10 rounds,
you gotta listen to me.


00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:32.310
You're dropping your
right hand, like that.


00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.945
Keep your head on his shoulder.


00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.280
- Can't you do that?
- Yeah.


00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:39.451
It's time for you to put this old man
down now. You do it now, hear?


00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:41.219
- Yes, sir.
- No more fooling around.


00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.155
That's enough of this nonsense.
You're young, man, and fast.


00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:46.859
Put him down so we can
go home, all right?


00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:54.266
Let's take a look,
Sailor. How's that eye?


00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.434
- Good, doc. It's good.
- Are you sure?


00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:57.669
- Yeah.
- All right.


00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.272
That opens up anymore,
I'm gonna stop the fight.


00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:03.545
- I'll do my best, doc.
- Do the best you can.


00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.411
Oh, great.


00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.980
Hey, King's fine. You check
that old man over there.


00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:11.957
- He ain't so fine.
- Back off, Cubby.


00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:15.687
- Looking better than Sailor.
- I'm fine.


00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:18.266
Didn't think you
could take a punch.


00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:21.295
- I can take a punch.
- You're proving it, kid.


00:09:22.862 --> 00:09:25.975
You're gonna get up close so
you can do some damage, okay?


00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:30.438
Concentrate.


00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.520
I wanna have it.


00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:41.022
You don't know what that means.


00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:43.489
Yes, I do.


00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:46.418
- No, you don't.
- It means work.


00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:48.687
It means money.


00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:52.131
- I can make money.
- How?


00:09:53.893 --> 00:09:56.266
Well, I can box.


00:09:57.663 --> 00:10:00.139
And I have some modeling jobs too.


00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:02.244
We're too young.


00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:07.678
- Too young for what?
- To have a baby.


00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.776
I wanna spend the rest
of my life with you.


00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:13.945
- No, you don't.
- Yes, I do.


00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:16.314
- No, you don't.
- I wanna marry you.


00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:20.725
I wanna marry you right
now. This morning.


00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:24.558
And I'll take care
of you and our baby.


00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:28.537
I promise you that.


00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.601
We have a family.


00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:37.948
I've never had that before.


00:10:40.573 --> 00:10:42.548
Me neither.


00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.682
Let's have our baby.


00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:54.797
Okay.


00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:57.960
Okay.


00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:00.230
Okay.


00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:04.263
But, King...


00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:10.412
I wanna give this baby
something besides life.


00:11:10.803 --> 00:11:12.277
What?


00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:17.479
I wanna give it something
it can be proud of.


00:11:19.612 --> 00:11:23.615
You keep him at a distance with
that jab. You dance around, huh?


00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:27.052
That man throws some wild
hooks, you know? Duck.


00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:30.021
Stop. You cannot win a fight
laying on a guy, okay?


00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:32.323
So let's win it. You
cannot outmuscle this kid.


00:11:32.324 --> 00:11:34.826
You cannot outfight him
and you can't outrun him.


00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:38.129
But you outweigh him and you can
outthink him. You wanna win it?


00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.398
- Yeah.
- You're the heavier one, lay on him.


00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:44.803
Keep your head on the right side of him.
Let the kid get cocky. Listen to me.


00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:47.572
Hey. Hey. What are you doing?


00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:50.208
What the hell's the matter?
You wanna win the fight?


00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:53.244
Keep your head on that right
shoulder. Once you get that rhythm,


00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:56.289
setup, he drops down,
you cross him, okay?


00:12:11.097 --> 00:12:15.166
Cubby. And what's this
I hear about King?


00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:17.635
I'm gonna give the
kid another chance.


00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:20.872
- King is a screwup.
- No, no, he's all cleaned up now.


00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:24.709
- The kid does have talent. Real talent.
- Yeah, he's always had talent.


00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.544
I poured a lot of money into him,


00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.980
and you gotta have it
to go with that talent.


00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:32.751
- Yeah, well, he's going to have a baby.
- There's a disaster waiting to happen.


00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:35.353
He got married to a
nice, young girl.


00:12:35.354 --> 00:12:37.789
He was my fighter before
you stole him from me.


00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.791
I did not steal him. Hey, look.


00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:42.293
You've got that night
coming up at the Lion Head?


00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:45.304
- Yeah.
- I want you to get King a fight there.


00:12:45.531 --> 00:12:48.466
- Maybe as an undercard.
- No, no, no, main event.


00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:53.071
- What? Look, King is no main event.
- Yes, he is.


00:12:53.072 --> 00:12:56.481
I'll put up the purse, man.
Ten-thousand dollars.


00:12:56.542 --> 00:12:57.742
Ten rounds.


00:12:57.743 --> 00:12:59.978
You really think he has
his head on straight?


00:12:59.979 --> 00:13:01.980
Yes. Yes, yes, yes.


00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:03.848
All right, I'll take
a piece of him.


00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:06.785
No, no, no. Ha, ha.
He doesn't like you.


00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:09.420
- I'll take 50 percent of him.
- He's not for sale.


00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:12.524
Hey, look, you know he was
my fighter before you took him.


00:13:12.525 --> 00:13:19.030
I didn't steal him. Hey, you know why
all your fighters leave you, man? Huh?


00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:21.432
- Because you steal them from me.
- Yeah.


00:13:21.433 --> 00:13:26.404
Same reason why your wife left you.
The same reason why I left you.


00:13:26.405 --> 00:13:28.640
Just give me a piece of the kid.


00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:30.377
Hey, look.


00:13:33.946 --> 00:13:36.514
You line up something for King, hm?


00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:39.184
Someone the kid could handle, huh?


00:13:39.185 --> 00:13:44.189
More than just a warm body,
but somebody he could beat, huh?


00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:46.057
I want it kept local.


00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:49.467
I don't wanna bear the expense
of bringing somebody in here.


00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:52.063
What about Charlie Simms?


00:13:52.064 --> 00:13:55.438
No, he's in prison. Armed robbery.


00:13:55.768 --> 00:13:57.368
Teddy Bigfoot?


00:13:57.369 --> 00:14:00.205
Teddy Bigfoot? Teddy Bigfoot,
man, he's a lot of Bigfoot.


00:14:00.206 --> 00:14:02.010
Man, he's 350 pounds now.


00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:06.177
- Bigfoot, yeah.
- Yeah.


00:14:06.178 --> 00:14:07.880
Hey.


00:14:08.514 --> 00:14:10.318
How about Sailor O'Connor?


00:14:10.382 --> 00:14:11.890
- Sailor?
- Yeah.


00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:14.129
Is he still fighting?


00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:17.188
No, but it might not really matter.


00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:20.191
I mean, if I could get him
to take one more fight.


00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:22.760
- People loved him.
- Yeah, yeah, he was very popular.


00:14:22.761 --> 00:14:25.630
Everybody wanted to see if he
was gonna get knocked down.


00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:28.132
- Yeah.
- And every fighter wanted to be the first.


00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:29.868
That's a good hook, man.


00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.769
Yeah, that'd be big if King


00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.039
could knock Sailor down. Heh.


00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.508
- That's good.
- Yeah. I'm gonna run it by King.


00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:39.110
- I'll talk to Sailor.
- Yup.


00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:42.547
- Hey, I want a piece of the kid.
- Not going to happen, man.


00:14:42.548 --> 00:14:45.483
- Well, we'll see.
- Yeah, yeah.


00:15:05.604 --> 00:15:07.784
<i>Why should we bother
to go see the doctor?</i>


00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.741
What's there to talk about?


00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:12.855
If you're dying, you're dying.
I know I'm dying.


00:15:15.014 --> 00:15:16.887
How do you know?


00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:22.557
Tell me you wouldn't know if you
were rotting from the inside out.


00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:28.793
It's cancer.


00:15:28.794 --> 00:15:32.339
Cancer, rot, no difference.


00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:33.666
Ma...


00:15:33.666 --> 00:15:38.136
Aw. Don't get all melancholy on me.


00:15:38.137 --> 00:15:41.306
I think it'd be good if you and I
went and saw a doctor together.


00:15:41.307 --> 00:15:45.512
- Yeah, well, you go see him if you want.
- Ma, there may be some pain.


00:15:47.813 --> 00:15:49.822
How long did he say I have?


00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:52.784
- Ma.
- Oh, don't be such a baby.


00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:54.726
How long did he say I have?


00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.164
Six months.


00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:04.104
I'm sorry.


00:16:05.264 --> 00:16:06.602
Sorry for what?


00:16:09.134 --> 00:16:11.814
No one's getting out alive.


00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:18.712
Is there anything I can do for you?


00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:27.697
Well, it might be nice to take one
last trip to Ireland before it comes.


00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.965
That'd be nice. Maybe you and me.


00:16:34.493 --> 00:16:36.195
Yeah.


00:16:44.503 --> 00:16:46.170
King, come on.


00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:48.351
Go box. Go box!


00:16:49.008 --> 00:16:50.448
Let's go home.


00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:31.549
<i>She's been in for five years.
She's asked me to be there</i>


00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.697
- for her parole hearing.
- You gonna go?


00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:36.589
I don't know.


00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:42.561
I've gotten to know her a lot better
through the letters that she sent me.


00:17:43.062 --> 00:17:46.402
She wants to speak with
you if she gets out.


00:17:47.032 --> 00:17:48.836
I can't do that.


00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:52.781
You can try.


00:17:54.173 --> 00:17:57.183
Sean, I don't have it in me.


00:17:59.812 --> 00:18:03.255
Sailor, her loss is
as great as yours.


00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:06.829
Is it?


00:18:07.853 --> 00:18:12.900
I'm sorry. Loss can't be measured.


00:18:13.859 --> 00:18:16.505
No. No, it can't.


00:18:18.931 --> 00:18:21.771
Do you want her to
continue to suffer?


00:18:29.074 --> 00:18:30.808
Do you


00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:34.047
want her to continue to suffer?


00:18:36.048 --> 00:18:38.922
Yeah. I think I do.


00:18:39.518 --> 00:18:41.595
Don't you think she's
suffered enough?


00:18:41.887 --> 00:18:46.661
Sean, I thought we agreed,
you can't measure suffering.


00:18:49.895 --> 00:18:53.076
Do you have no pity for her?


00:18:53.765 --> 00:18:57.503
You know, my ma has a
saying about pity:


00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:01.606
Pity arrests the heart


00:19:01.607 --> 00:19:04.344
and unites it with those
who have wronged us.


00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.415
I need to go see Rose.


00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.648
Won't do any good,
she's at war with God.


00:19:10.649 --> 00:19:12.294
Yeah.


00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:17.121
You taking confessions
today, Father?


00:19:17.122 --> 00:19:19.632
You have nothing to confess,


00:19:19.725 --> 00:19:23.027
other than what we
just talked about.


00:19:29.301 --> 00:19:30.946
Yes.


